---
title: "Accordion"
description: "Collapsible sections built on native details and summary elements. Works without JavaScript."
tags: [disclosure, css]
usage: |
  Wrap one or more `<details>` elements in an element with the `accordion` class.
  Each `<summary>` is the clickable heading.

  - Give the `<details>` elements the same `name` attribute to allow only one open
    section at a time.
  - Add `open` to a `<details>` to expand it on load.
accessibility: |
  - Native `<details>` and `<summary>` are keyboard operable (Enter and Space) and
    announce their expanded state, so no ARIA is needed.
  - Keep summary text short; it is the accessible name of the toggle.
  - The open and close animation is skipped when the person prefers reduced
    motion.
customProperties:
  "--accordion-border": "Border around each section."
  "--accordion-radius": "Corner radius of each section."
  "--accordion-padding": "Padding of the summary and content."
  "--accordion-summary-gap": "Space between the marker and the summary text."
  "--accordion-summary-font-weight": "Font weight of the summary."
  "--accordion-marker": "Character shown before the summary; it rotates when open."
  "--accordion-duration": "Length of the open and close animation."
  "--accordion-easing": "Timing function of the animation."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<div class="accordion">
  <details name="faq" open>
    <summary>What is vanillapod?</summary>
    <p>A collection of vanilla web components and DOM utilities.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Does it need a framework?</summary>
    <p>No, it only uses platform features.</p>
  </details>
</div>
